  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results achieved</narrative>
    <narrative xml:lang="SV">Uppn&#xe5;dda resultat</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Anti-Corruption Commission has developed practical tools with the aim of supporting significant reduction in corruption risks through implementation of preventive measures, and by training of key public officials. The Integrity Red has been strengthened, and common policies have been formulated to report suspected corruption.

The 2024-2028 General Government Policy has been strengthened by incorporating guidelines that promote the active participation of Indigenous peoples, women, and other vulnerable groups in decision-making processes. This inclusive and strategic approach ensures that policies respond to the needs of the entire population, promoting equity in government actions and laying the foundations for a new social contract for the 2024-2028 period.

As a result of the implementation of a strategic management methodology aimed at achieving presidential goals through the SIGOB METAS System, 41 road maps were created for various government interventions, 22 of which now report directly to the presidency, facilitating direct and effective monitoring of progress.

The project has facilitated the implementation of the Vice Presidency Management Center, a planning and coordination mechanism aimed at strengthening the management capacities of the Vice Presidency of the Republic of Guatemala, aligning it with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), particularly SDG 16, which promotes peace, justice, and the building of strong institutions.</narrative>
   </description>
